arXiv:2611.11908v1 Announce Type: new 
Abstract: In this paper, we study the Schr\"{o}dinger-Maxwell equation with critical growth and mass subcritical perturbation
  \begin{align*}
  \begin{cases}
  \displaystyle - \Delta u+\lambda u+ \left(|x|^{-1}\ast| u|^2\right) u
  =|u|^{4}u +|u|^{p-2}u\quad\quad \text{in} \ \mathbb{ R}^3,
  \displaystyle \int_{\mathbb{R}^3}|u|^2dx=a^2,
  \end{cases}
  \end{align*} where $a>0$ is prescribed, $3<p<\frac{10}{3}$, $\ast$ denotes the convolution and $\lambda\in \mathbb{R}$ appears as a Lagrange multiplier. When the nonlocal convolution term is absent, the above equation can be reduced to the Schr\"{o}dinger equation. In this case, the previous works showed that it admits a local minimizer (ground-state) and a mountain-pass type solution. By contrast, we surprisingly find that the above equation has no solutions with negative energy provided $a>0$ is sufficiently small. More precisely, we rigorously prove that the above equation possesses a mountain-pass type solution with positive energy for sufficiently small $a>0$, which reveals an essential difference in solution structure between the Schr\"{o}dinger-Maxwell equation and the classical Schr\"{o}dinger equation in the parameter range $3<p<\frac{10}{3}$. The main difficulty encountered in this work is the loss of compactness arising from the Sobolev critical term. Furthermore, we explore the dynamical properties of the corresponding time-dependent problem and establish the strong instability of its standing wave solutions. It is worth pointing out that this work refines and extends the existing literature by covering the unexplored parameter regime $p\in(3,\frac{10}{3})$.

arXiv:2504.18750v2 Announce Type: replace 
Abstract: We consider the weakly coupled elliptic system of logistic type, \begin{equation}
  \begin{cases}
  -\Delta u &=\mu_1u- |u|^{p-2}u+ \beta |u|^{\frac{p}{2}-2}u |v|{^{\frac{p}{2}}}\mbox{ in }\Omega,
  -\Delta v & =\mu_2 v- |v|^{p-2}v+\beta |u|^{\frac{p}{2}}|v|^{\frac{p}{2}-2}v \mbox{ in }\Omega,
  \ \ u,v &\in H_0^1(\Omega),
  \end{cases} \end{equation}
  where $\Omega\subset\mathbb{R}^N$ is a bounded connected domain with $N\geq 2$, $2< p < 2^*$, $\lambda_1(\Omega)< \mu_1\leq\mu_2$, and $\lambda_1(\Omega)$ denotes the first eigenvalue of the Laplacian operator in $\Omega$ with Dirichlet boundary conditions. We say the system is competitive if $\beta<0$ and cooperative if $\beta>0$, for $\beta \in \mathbb{R}$.
  We prove the existence and multiplicity of solutions to the problem \eqref{LS} in alternative variational frameworks, depending on the range of the parameter $\beta.$ We do not rely on bifurcation or degree theory, which have been used in the literature for logistic-type problems. Instead, the novelty is to obtain min-max type solutions by exploiting the different geometry of the functional associated with the logistic problem. In case $N\geq 2$, we establish existence and multiplicity results for different ranges of the coupling parameter, considering both the case \(2<p<4\) and the classical case \(p=4\). We also investigate the asymptotic behavior of selected solutions as \(\beta\to1^-\) and \(\beta\to-\infty\).}
  \textsc{Key words: Logistic System, Ground State Solution, Linking structure, Seminodal Solution.}{\small}
  \textsc{MSC 2020: } {\small 35J15 35J20, 35J60, 62J12.}
